%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: state level agencies
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: Which state-level body is considered the nodal agency for academic
      and training matters in school education?
    Options:
    - State Board of Education
    - State Council of Educational Research and Training (SCERT)
    - Directorate of Education
    - State University
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The primary role of the State Directorate of Education in in-service
      teacher education is:'
    Options:
    - Conducting academic research
    - Training master trainers
    - Developing training modules
    - Administrative implementation and providing logistical support
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: The SCERT is to the state as the _____ is to the nation.
    Options:
    - UGC
    - NCERT
    - NCTE
    - CBSE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which state-level institution is primarily responsible for adapting
      the National Curriculum Framework (NCF) to the local context?
    Options:
    - The State Board of Examination
    - The SCERT
    - The District Institute of Education and Training (DIET)
    - The Municipal Corporation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A key function of the SCERT is to:'
    Options:
    - Recruit teachers for private schools
    - Manage the state's finances
    - Set the syllabus for university education
    - Plan and coordinate in-service teacher education programs across the state
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which body is responsible for conducting training programs for
      paper setters and evaluators of state board examinations?
    Options:
    - SCERT
    - State Board of School Education
    - Directorate of Education
    - CRC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The institution that provides academic and administrative guidance
      to DIETs in a state is the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - SCERT
    - CRC
    - BRC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a primary function of the State Directorate
      of Education?
    Options:
    - Developing textbooks
    - Awarding Ph.D. degrees
    - Conducting action research in classrooms
    - Releasing funds for teacher training programs
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A workshop for master trainers on a new state education policy
      would most likely be organized by the:'
    Options:
    - Block Resource Centre (BRC)
    - SCERT
    - Cluster Resource Centre (CRC)
    - Village Education Committee
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "S" in SIE stands for:'
    Options:
    - School
    - State
    - Science
    - Social
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which state-level agency would be responsible for developing a
      handbook on inclusive education practices for teachers across the state?
    Options:
    - The State Police Department
    - The District Magistrate's office
    - The State Transport Corporation
    - The SCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The administrative head of school education in a state is typically
      the:'
    Options:
    - Director of Education
    - Principal of a DIET
    - Chief Minister
    - Governor
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher wishing to pursue an M.Ed. degree while in service would
      enroll in a:'
    Options:
    - DIET
    - State University's Department of Education
    - BRC
    - SCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: The main target group for the State Board of School Education's
      training programs are teachers of which levels?
    Options:
    - Pre-primary only
    - Elementary only
    - Secondary and Senior Secondary (Classes 9-12)
    - University level
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The SCERT''s role in research is primarily to:'
    Options:
    - Conduct medical research
    - Investigate state-specific educational problems and solutions
    - Develop new software for industries
    - Study astronomical phenomena
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which institution acts as the bridge between the NCERT and the
      district-level agencies (DIETs)?
    Options:
    - The Central Government
    - The SCERT
    - The Local School
    - The Village Panchayat
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The development of state-specific textbooks is a key function
      of the:'
    Options:
    - Directorate of Education
    - State Board
    - SCERT
    - National Library
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A "State Institute of Science Education" focuses specifically
      on the professional development of:'
    Options:
    - Language teachers
    - Science and Mathematics teachers
    - Social Studies teachers
    - Physical Education teachers
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The primary source of academic leadership for all elementary and
      secondary teacher education in a state is the:'
    Options:
    - Chief Secretary
    - SCERT
    - District Collector
    - High Court
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is NOT a function of the SCERT?
    Options:
    - Organizing cultural festivals
    - Designing in-service teacher education curriculum
    - Conducting educational surveys
    - Organizing advanced training for teacher educators
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "C" in SCERT stands for:'
    Options:
    - Central
    - Council
    - College
    - Commission
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A major state-level initiative for integrated teacher training
      launched in many states is:'
    Options:
    - NISHTHA
    - NASA
    - WHO
    - UNICEF
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The state-level body that ensures that the policies planned by
      the SCERT are implemented on the ground is the:'
    Options:
    - Directorate of Education
    - State Legal Services Authority
    - State Election Commission
    - State Sports Council
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher seeking a promotion based on in-service training qualifications
      would have their records verified by the:'
    Options:
    - SCERT
    - Directorate of Education
    - School Principal
    - Local Police Station
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The creation of SCERTs was strongly recommended by the:'
    Options:
    - Indian Constitution
    - Kothari Commission (1964-66)
    - National Policy on Information Technology
    - National Health Policy
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which state-level institution is most directly involved in the
      academic supervision of DIETs?
    Options:
    - The State Board
    - The BRC
    - The CRC
    - The SCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A program aimed at training all DIET faculty in the state on a
      new pedagogical approach would be organized by the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - SCERT
    - District Education Officer
    - Block Development Officer
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "E" in SCERT stands for:'
    Options:
    - Economic
    - Elementary
    - Educational
    - Environmental
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: A key difference between the SCERT and the Directorate of Education
      is that the SCERT focuses on _____ while the Directorate focuses on _____.
    Options:
    - administration; academics
    - academics; administration
    - finance; research
    - law; teaching
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which agency is responsible for the final approval of state-level
      textbooks developed by the SCERT?
    Options:
    - The State Government
    - The NCERT
    - The District Magistrate
    - The Village Sarpanch
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The state-level structure ensures that in-service teacher education
      is:'
    Options:
    - Isolated from national goals
    - Aligned with both national frameworks and state-specific needs
    - Identical in all states without any variation
    - Managed solely by private entities
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A "Refresher Course" for secondary school teachers is often organized
      by:'
    Options:
    - SCERT or a University's Department of Education
    - The Cluster Resource Centre (CRC)
    - The Anganwadi worker
    - The Town Council
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "R" in SCERT stands for:'
    Options:
    - Reform
    - Research
    - Regional
    - Rural
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A major challenge for state-level agencies is:'
    Options:
    - Lack of any educational policies to implement
    - Having too few teachers to train
    - The absence of a national-level guiding body
    - Ensuring equity and quality in training across all districts
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate goal of the SCERT''s activities is to:'
    Options:
    - Increase the number of government employees
    - Enhance the quality of classroom teaching and learning in the state
    - Promote a single political party
    - Reduce the state's education budget
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which state-level body would be involved in the process of recognizing
      teacher education institutions?
    Options:
    - SCERT (in an advisory capacity to NCTE)
    - State Transport Authority
    - State Electricity Board
    - State Tourism Department
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The academic resource person for a state-level workshop on ''Activity-Based
      Learning'' would most likely be from the:'
    Options:
    - SCERT
    - Fire Station
    - State Bank of India
    - Local grocery store
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The development of a state-level achievement test to monitor learning
      outcomes is a function of the:'
    Options:
    - SCERT
    - State Health Department
    - Public Works Department
    - State Agriculture University
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The relationship between the SCERT and the NCERT is best described
      as:'
    Options:
    - Competitive and independent
    - A hierarchical one where the SCERT guides the NCERT
    - A collaborative one where the NCERT provides a framework and the SCERT adapts
      it
    - Non-existent
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A "State Institute of Education (SIE)" typically focuses on:'
    Options:
    - Higher Education
    - Elementary Education
    - Technical Education
    - Medical Education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which state-level institution is responsible for the in-service
      training of teacher educators?
    Options:
    - DIET
    - SCERT
    - CRC
    - BRC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The "T" in SCERT stands for:'
    Options:
    - Teaching
    - Tertiary
    - Technology
    - Training
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A university''s Department of Education contributes to in-service
      education primarily through:'
    Options:
    - Organizing primary health check-up camps
    - Offering advanced degree programs and conducting research
    - Managing school infrastructure
    - Distributing free uniforms to students
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The success of state-level in-service education programs is most
      evident in the:'
    Options:
    - Number of meetings held in the state capital
    - Improved academic performance and teaching practices across the state's schools
    - Size of the SCERT building
    - Number of cars owned by officials
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: Which body is responsible for monitoring the utilization of funds
      allocated for teacher training by the central government?
    Options:
    - The State Directorate of Education
    - The SCERT
    - The Lok Sabha
    - The Supreme Court
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher who develops an innovative teaching method may get state-level
      recognition through the:'
    Options:
    - Income Tax Department
    - State Pollution Control Board
    - Motor Vehicles Department
    - SCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The state-level planning for in-service teacher education under
      the Samagra Shiksha scheme is coordinated by the:'
    Options:
    - SCERT and Directorate of Education
    - District Collector
    - Municipal Commissioner
    - State Police Chief
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'A key role of the State Board in in-service education is to:'
    Options:
    - Develop pre-service teacher education curriculum
    - Orient teachers on examination reforms and evaluation processes
    - Construct school buildings
    - Appoint university professors
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
  - QuestionText: 'The academic autonomy of the SCERT allows it to:'
    Options:
    - Ignore national educational goals
    - Adapt programs to meet the specific linguistic and cultural needs of the state
    - Set foreign policy for the state
    - Print currency
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: state level agencies
